# XSH tcgetpgrp()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Tests with a controlling terminal build their own session: a child calls
# setsid() and opens the subsidiary side of a pseudo-terminal (XSI) without
# O_NOCTTY; whether that makes it the controlling terminal is
# implementation-defined (XBD 11.1.3), so the test is UNRESOLVED unless the
# path returned by ctermid() can then be opened. A second child in its own
# process group (not orphaned, its parent being the session leader) is the
# background caller. Everything is bounded by alarm() and reaped.
#
# "when BASE|XSI": the requirements are Base; XSI is named only so that the
# driver builds these tests with the XSI feature macro (the pseudo-terminal
# set-up needs it). They run wherever they build, and a set-up that is not
# available is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.001
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcgetpgrp(-1) and tcgetpgrp() of a closed descriptor return -1
           with EBADF; ENOTTY is also accepted when the process has no
           controlling terminal that the ctermid() pathname opens (both
           errors then apply, XSH 2.3).
test       t/001-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.002
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcgetpgrp() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a
           pipe and /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/002-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.003
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.3
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a session leader whose controlling terminal has just been
           acquired, tcgetpgrp() on that terminal returns the process
           group ID of the session leader.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/003-fg-initial.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.004
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcgetpgrp() called from a process in a background process group
           (not orphaned) on its controlling terminal returns the
           foreground group ID (the session leader's) and the process is
           not stopped.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/004-from-background.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.005
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.2
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       After the foreground group (set with tcsetpgrp()) has no
           process left, tcgetpgrp() returns a value greater than 1 that
           is not the ID of any existing process group (kill(-value, 0)
           fails with ESRCH).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. The set-up
           uses tcsetpgrp(); a failure there is UNRESOLVED.
timeout    40
test       t/005-no-fg-group.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.006
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a process that has no controlling terminal (it called
           setsid() and opened the terminal with O_NOCTTY), tcgetpgrp() on
           a pseudo-terminal subsidiary descriptor returns -1 with ENOTTY.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/006-enotty-no-ctty.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetpgrp.007
anchor     functions/tcgetpgrp.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a process whose controlling terminal is one pseudo-terminal,
           tcgetpgrp() on the subsidiary descriptor of a different pseudo-
           terminal (opened with O_NOCTTY) returns -1 with ENOTTY.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
timeout    40
test       t/007-enotty-other-tty.c
